  "meta": {
    "title": "Why Europe Is Warmer Than Canada at the Same Latitude 🌊🔥❄️",
    "description": "London 🇬🇧 is further north than most of Canada's big cities, so why is it so much milder? 🤔 A big part of the answer is the Gulf Stream 🌊 a warm, fast current that starts in the Gulf of Mexico, runs up the US coast and crosses the Atlantic as the North Atlantic Current. It carries about 30 million cubic metres of water per second through the Florida Straits, more than all the rivers flowing into the Atlantic combined 🤯 That's why Norway's coast can stay ice-free so close to the Arctic.",
    "pinnedComment": [
      "A river in the ocean that heats up Europe 🌊🔥",
      "Did you know this about the Gulf Stream? 👇",
      "Which ocean secret next? 🗺️"
    ],
